"https://github.com/SakuyaCN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T12:01:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T12:01:47Z","body":"If the method being called has a parameter that is a callback, and this callback is a custom interface, do I need to implement this interface at the Java level and then use JavaClassWrapper?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2647785738/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648191654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99492#issuecomment-2648191654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99492","id":2648191654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d2DKm","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T14:37:10Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T16:04:33Z","body":"@SakuyaCN To implement an interface, you'd have to do it on the Java side. `JavaClassWrapper` only lets you call methods or create instances of already existing classes, not define new ones.\r\n\r\nAnd if you're going to do some stuff on the Java side (with a [Godot Android plugin](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/platform/android/android_plugin.html)) then, depending on your needs, you may want to do everything that way and not use `JavaClassWrapper` at all. The primary goal of `JavaClassWrapper` is to allow you to do simple things from GDScript/C# without having to switch to the Java side.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648191654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648481755","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99492#issuecomment-2648481755","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99492","id":2648481755,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d3J_b","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T15:55:45Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T15:55:45Z","body":"> If the method being called has a parameter that is a callback, and this callback is a custom interface, do I need to implement this interface at the Java level and then use JavaClassWrapper?\r\n\r\n@SakuyaCN Can you provide some sample code (pseudo-code is fine) to illustrate what you are asking?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648481755/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649846923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99492#issuecomment-2649846923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99492","id":2649846923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d8XSL","user":{"login":"SakuyaCN","id":26734975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzM0OTc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26734975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN","html_url":"https://github.com/SakuyaCN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SakuyaCN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T05:43:08Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T05:43:08Z","body":"> > 如果被调用的方法有一个作为回调的参数，并且这个回调是一个自定义接口，我是否需要在 Java 级别实现这个接口，然后使用 JavaClassWrapper？\r\n> \r\n> 您能否提供一些示例代码（伪代码也可以）来说明您所问的问题？\r\n\r\nOf course, assuming I have a method whose parameter is an interface, calling this method would require implementing an inner class:\r\n\r\nkotlin\r\n`\r\nTest.registerCallback(object :Callback{\r\n     override fun onResult(code: Int) {}})\r\n`\r\n\r\nMy current approach is to implement the interface in Java code, then initialize it using JavaClassWrapper, and pass it as a parameter.\r\n\r\ngdscrpit\r\n```\r\nvar callback= JavaClassWrapper.wrap('com.godot.game.BaseCallback')\r\nvar instance = callback.call('<init>')\r\n\r\nTest.registerCallback(instance)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf this functionality can be achieved, it would significantly streamline the process of creating plugins.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649846923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649859124","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99492#issuecomment-2649859124","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99492","id":2649859124,"